# DTF tier manifest: bounded-memory-streaming
#   (artifact-keeper#4924, #5126, #5336, #5364, #5133, #5130; all fixed on
#   main for 1.12.0. #5130 is also on 1.11.13 through the 1.11.x cherry-pick
#   d49b5817, so its red image is the main build sha-ad20810.)
# Profile-set: filesystem + logging.json-file (the #5130 startup line is read
# with `docker logs`) + limits.memory: the backend container is capped at
# LIMITS_MEMORY (768m) with no swap. Only this slot's backend is capped; the
# cap only ever lowers what it may use. Every fixture is random bytes made at
# run time (nothing large is committed) and every pass is checked against a
# sha256.
#
# THE BUGS
# #5126  Hosted members of a PyPI virtual served without a presigned
#        redirect (filesystem, or S3 without presign) went through
#        `read_local_content`: the whole wheel was read into memory per
#        concurrent request.
# #5364  Hosted Conan recipe/package file downloads used `storage.get` +
#        `Body::from`, and uploads buffered the whole body: memory grew with
#        the sum of the package files in flight (a CI burst OOM-killed the
#        pod at 6 GiB).
# #5336  Backup read every artifact into a Vec, gzipped the archive into a
#        second buffer and cloned it; restore loaded the .tar.gz and
#        decompressed every entry into memory before writing.
# #5133  The final `PUT ?digest=` of a whole-body OCI layer push re-read,
#        rehashed and rewrote the layer and copied it again before sending
#        the response headers, so finalize time grew with the layer
#        (containerd gives it 30 s). The old path streams, so it does not
#        OOM; the observable is the re-read itself.
# #4924  A cold `repomd.xml` render of a hosted RPM root loaded every row's
#        metadata JSON and built each uncompressed document in memory.
# #5130  The published image was glibc malloc, which keeps freed burst
#        memory in per-thread arenas (RSS ratchets up and OOMs). Only the
#        allocator facet is gated: no RSS-over-time assertion.
#
# THE GATES (each FIX case: the backend must be the same process at the end
# of the case, i.e. not OOM-killed, and every byte must match)
#   (CONTROL) on every image: 1 MiB files round-trip through the PyPI
#             virtual, hosted Conan and an OCI blob push; a 1 GiB layer
#             (more than the cap) pushed as one whole-body PUT is 201 and
#             pulls byte-exact (the upload streams on both images).
#   (FIX)     #5130 the first `Global allocator:` startup line says jemalloc
#                   (red sha-ad20810: `system`);
#             #5133 the backend process reads < 1/8 of the layer
#                   (/proc/1/io rchar) between the last body byte and the 201
#                   of that whole-body PUT (red: 2048 MiB for a 1024 MiB
#                   layer; green: 0);
#             #5126 8 parallel GETs (16 MB/s each, so they overlap) of a
#                   160 MiB hosted wheel through the virtual, all byte-exact;
#             #5364 8 parallel GETs of a 160 MiB conan_package.tgz, and a
#                   1 GiB conan_package.tgz upload is 201 and downloads
#                   byte-exact (red: 413, the buffered body is refused
#                   against the cgroup budget);
#             #5336 a backup of 6 x 160 MiB artifacts completes (count 6);
#                   then, with the stored objects removed, a restore of the
#                   artifacts completes and all 6 download byte-exact. When
#                   the capped backup fails (red), the archive is taken with
#                   the cap raised to BMS_HELPER_MEMORY (6g) and the backend
#                   is restarted under the cap again, so the restore is still
#                   judged under 768m;
#             #4924 1000 synthetic packages (419 MiB of file-list metadata,
#                   seeded straight into Postgres, the
#                   artifact-keeper-test#621 approach) in an
#                   `repodata_mode: on_request` root; with the cap raised to
#                   BMS_RPM_MEMORY (3g) a cold repomd.xml is 200 and
#                   primary/filelists list every package and match the
#                   checksums repomd.xml advertises. Last case: it leaves the
#                   cap raised. The fixed render still peaks at ~0.8-1.3 GiB
#                   anon here (about 670 MiB plus ~1x the metadata), so it
#                   cannot run under 768m; 1.11.13 needs more than 4 GiB.
#
# Sampled peak anonymous memory (cgroup memory.stat) is printed per case as a
# note; memory.peak is not used, it counts reclaimable page cache.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: many admin and download requests back to back.
COVERS="4924 5126 5336 5364 5133 5130"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem logging.json-file limits.memory"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
export LIMITS_MEMORY="${LIMITS_MEMORY:-768m}"
